    "F0 actual ABI entry is 0x011a5438, not index interior 0x011a5444. It loads remaining/cursor and constant 0x7edc before the indexed extent.",
    "Stored-line actual ABI entry is 0x011a5470, not index interior 0x011a5478. It initializes the source-index offsets before the indexed extent.",
    "Secondary setup coefficients are unsigned halfwords, passed in r2. Ghidra omits that third argument.",
    "Mode-two scan initialization tests height bit 1 (height & 2), not parity.",
    "Register shifts consume low eight shift bits; LSL >=32 is zero; ASR >=32 replicates sign.",
    "set_scale adds 128 before signed truncation by 256; refresh_scales does not.",
    "Short/byte axis line-to uses destination-x as the destination-y index; rotated line-to uses destination-y."
  ],
  "consumerLaws": [
    "VM belongs to context at context+0xb8; otherwise byte-reader progress does not update the interpreter remaining field.",
    "Font bytecode storage and VM workspace are disjoint under the original font/context producers.",
    "Nibble point indices range 0..15; original coefficient/setup producer counts must fit their eight-value and sixteen-point ABI storage.",
    "The verified closed opcode table returns only 0,0x8003,0x8004. The stock low-halfword 0xffff handler-result branch is unreachable for these bodies; InstructionSignal carries the reachable states.",
    "Public root accepts raw original mode bits. Modes other than zero and two emit coordinate triples through the owned draw-curve helper.",
    "Mode-two height 1,5,... leaves the final row unchanged during grid initialization. Fixtures assert preservation; no synthetic initialization or missing-data success is introduced.",
    "Original bytecode readers do not validate per-instruction remaining lengths. Underfilled programs can read beyond their declared bytecode extent; malformed-input models supply explicit mapped bytes and do not claim bounds safety."
